    "created_at": "2019-06-05T22:52:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-06-05T22:54:22Z",
    "body": "> developers with access to their backend code\r\n\r\nAs Feature-Policies generally control front-end behavior, this seems especially worrying.\r\n\r\nMy biggest take away from the fact that [98% of devs, when given a choice, enabled Client Hints using HTML rather than HTTP](https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-feature-policy/issues/55#issuecomment-406627096), was not that Client Hints need HTML delivery, but rather that front-end-developers do.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
